  "rationale": "The spec requires >=1 MSPS throughput and max_abs_err <= 2^-10, with area minimization as the primary objective. The iterative family is excluded because it produces only 1 result every N+3 cycles, making it very hard to reach 1 MSPS without extremely high Fmax, and it will likely be dominated on area by pipelined variants. The three pipelined/unrolled families are the viable candidates. pipelined_m is the most promising because it balances FF count (area) against throughput by registering every m stages. unrolled_k is a strong alternative that may use fewer FFs than pipelined_m for the same accuracy. pipelined is included as a reference to map the full Pareto front. Parameter ranges are focused: data_width 12-16 and n_iter 10-14 should be sufficient to meet the 2^-10 accuracy constraint (accuracy_bits >= 10) while keeping area low. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept minimal to reduce datapath width. The budget is split to explore the trade-offs between these families, with emphasis on pipelined_m and unrolled_k where the area/throughput/accuracy balance is most favorable."
}

